    "text": "satisfied; but so long as any part of the demand remains due, you are at liberty to sue the others notwithstanding you have obtained judgment against one. This, I think, establishes the principle, that where there is a joint obligation and a separate one also, you do not, by recovering judgment against one, preclude yourself from suing the other \".",
